WEBVTT

00:00:10.100 --> 00:00:19.900
<b>LEGEND</b>

00:00:10.100 --> 00:00:19.900
<b>OF THE</b>

00:00:10.100 --> 00:00:19.900
<b>  GALACTIC HEROES</b>

00:01:39.800 --> 00:01:44.370
Chapter 3

00:01:39.800 --> 00:01:44.370
One Hundred Billion Stars, One Hundred Billion Lights

00:02:17.250 --> 00:02:22.480
I'd like to find our regimental commander before I become a white-haired old man, or at least his body.

00:02:22.480 --> 00:02:25.150
I don't care if
he's dead or alive.

00:02:25.150 --> 00:02:26.150
Don't you agree, Lt. Colonel ?

00:02:39.090 --> 00:02:42.650
Walter von Schenkopp
is 30 years old.

00:02:42.650 --> 00:02:48.290
Since he disliked the military academy's atmosphere he attended the professional ground warfare school.

00:02:49.590 --> 00:02:52.830
He entered the war at the
age of 18 as a corporal.

00:02:52.830 --> 00:02:55.850
Then he garnered accolades and
got promoted at the age of 20.

00:02:55.850 --> 00:03:01.300
At the age of 21, he was recommended to attend officer's school.

00:03:01.300 --> 00:03:05.300
He finished the curriculum
at the age of 22...

00:03:05.300 --> 00:03:08.860
...and was assigned to the Rosenritter
Regiment as a 2nd Lieutenant.

00:03:08.860 --> 00:03:11.360
Since then, he has continued to garner
accolades and was promoted to Lt. Colonel...

00:03:11.360 --> 00:03:14.890
...and regimental vice-commander
while he was still in his 20's.

00:03:14.890 --> 00:03:19.550
If the current regimental commander,
Colonel Wahnschaffe, dies...

00:03:19.550 --> 00:03:24.950
...Schenkopp is next in line to become the
13th regimental commander of the Rosenritter.

00:03:52.680 --> 00:03:53.610
Enemy sighted.

00:03:53.610 --> 00:03:55.330
10 km ahead, at 11 o'clock.

00:03:56.220 --> 00:03:58.160
I'll bring up the images
from the land gopher.

00:04:14.210 --> 00:04:15.520
What is it ?

00:04:15.520 --> 00:04:17.000
Actually...

00:04:19.200 --> 00:04:23.780
...I think I recognized someone
among the enemy troops.

00:04:23.780 --> 00:04:25.930
But I'm not certain, so...

00:04:26.540 --> 00:04:28.350
Why would you recognize him ?

00:04:30.520 --> 00:04:34.220
It was the previous regimental
commander, Colonel Luneberg.

00:04:46.010 --> 00:04:50.750
He was the previous commander
of the Rosenritter ?

00:04:50.750 --> 00:04:51.550
Yes, sir.

00:04:51.550 --> 00:04:55.440
Three years ago, he defected back to the
Empire from the Free Planets Alliance.

00:04:56.120 --> 00:05:03.000
Until then, he was a Colonel in the Alliance Forces and 11th regimental commander of the Rosenritter.

00:05:03.720 --> 00:05:08.310
So that's why he knows so 
much about the rebel forces.

00:05:08.310 --> 00:05:11.980
And he's got reasons to be confident about his ground warfare skills.

00:05:11.980 --> 00:05:15.850
He's considered to be
a master of close combat.

00:05:15.850 --> 00:05:21.900
It's strange that someone of such caliber
was only promoted once in three years.

00:05:22.960 --> 00:05:26.550
Usually, defectors from the
Alliance are treated favorably...

00:05:26.550 --> 00:05:29.620
...as they're good sources
of political propaganda.

00:05:29.620 --> 00:05:33.160
On that subject, there's a
rumor that he's not well liked...

00:05:33.160 --> 00:05:40.690
...because he married a beautiful lady of
distinguished lineage upon his defection.

00:05:41.300 --> 00:05:42.220
Really ?

00:05:42.220 --> 00:05:44.700
It's only a rumor.

00:05:47.600 --> 00:05:51.390
Whatever the reason, it's certain
he's not treated favorably.

00:05:52.130 --> 00:05:58.130
After all, he was assigned
to the Grimmelshausen Fleet.

00:05:58.130 --> 00:06:02.600
Commodore Luneberg himself
is leading the ground troops.

00:06:02.600 --> 00:06:06.280
What do you think of
his leadership skills ?

00:06:06.280 --> 00:06:08.150
He's capable.

00:06:08.150 --> 00:06:11.040
His troops are orderly, too.

00:06:11.840 --> 00:06:13.830
But I hate him.

00:06:14.890 --> 00:06:21.270
I want to clarify, Kircheis, that
I only hate him as a human being.

00:06:21.270 --> 00:06:24.940
I'm not belittling
him as a commander.

00:06:24.940 --> 00:06:28.530
Yes, I know, Lord Reinhard.

00:06:34.740 --> 00:06:37.150
Colonel Luneberg...

00:06:38.990 --> 00:06:41.310
...it's an irony, isn't it,
to meet in a place like this ?

00:06:41.310 --> 00:06:43.480
It's not a coincidence, though.

00:06:43.480 --> 00:06:48.320
Since combat between the Alliance and Empire
is largely restricted to the Iserlohn Corridor...

00:06:48.320 --> 00:06:52.850
...and the opportunities for
ground battles are limited...

00:06:52.850 --> 00:06:56.050
...the probability of meeting
him isn't particularly low.

00:06:56.050 --> 00:06:57.570
You're right, but...

00:06:58.770 --> 00:07:01.500
This might lead to
adverse conditions.

00:07:05.120 --> 00:07:06.890
What are we going
to do, Lt. Colonel ?

00:07:07.290 --> 00:07:09.110
We'll adhere to common sense.

00:07:09.110 --> 00:07:12.340
Try to find our allies without
being found by the enemy.

00:07:12.340 --> 00:07:13.660
It's that simple.

00:07:13.660 --> 00:07:14.700
Y...yes.

00:07:22.430 --> 00:07:27.710
Siegfried Kircheis continued to
investigate Luneberg's background.

00:07:27.710 --> 00:07:31.100
That's because Reinhard would
want capable people as his allies.

00:07:32.200 --> 00:07:37.890
Whether Luneberg would aid the
realization of Reinhard's ambition...

00:07:37.890 --> 00:07:41.500
...or become an obstacle to it...

00:07:41.500 --> 00:07:46.030
...Kircheis would have to know more
about him to make a judgment.

00:07:49.600 --> 00:07:55.470
The lady whom Luneberg married
is a sister of Count Hartenberg.

00:07:55.470 --> 00:07:59.390
She's 26 years of age - nine
years younger than Luneberg.

00:07:59.390 --> 00:08:05.200
She was engaged to another aristocrat,
but he died in the war against the Alliance.

00:08:06.230 --> 00:08:09.550
Afterwards, she rejected
several marriage proposals...

00:08:09.550 --> 00:08:14.700
...but Luneberg made a rather forceful proposal and they finally married a year ago.

00:08:16.450 --> 00:08:21.400
It is said that Count Hartenberg promoted the
marriage to save her from her deep sorrow...

00:08:21.400 --> 00:08:27.240
...but it was rumored that Luneberg took an ungentlemanly path to realize this marriage.

00:08:32.520 --> 00:08:38.810
If Lord Reinhard finds this out,
he'll hate Luneberg even more.

00:08:52.390 --> 00:08:54.050
Lt. Colonel, please
take a look at this.

00:08:55.760 --> 00:08:57.640
It must be ours, right ?

00:08:58.210 --> 00:09:01.550
They're still fresh.
They must be nearby.

00:09:01.550 --> 00:09:03.100
Alright.
Let's follow them.

00:09:15.720 --> 00:09:17.160
Hasn't it been fixed yet ?

00:09:17.160 --> 00:09:18.010
No, sir.

00:09:18.010 --> 00:09:18.990
Actually...

00:09:18.990 --> 00:09:21.380
The shaft is broken.

00:09:21.380 --> 00:09:24.280
Unless we replace the
part, we can't move.

00:09:24.280 --> 00:09:27.140
What happened with the
pre-departure maintenance ?

00:09:27.140 --> 00:09:32.750
I don't mean to argue, but recently, the
quality of supplies has been inferior, and...

00:09:32.750 --> 00:09:33.880
I don't need excuses !

00:09:34.950 --> 00:09:36.420
Just get it fixed !

00:09:36.420 --> 00:09:37.090
Yes, sir !

00:09:37.490 --> 00:09:40.730
What an asshole.  It's not
something we can fix here.

00:09:41.960 --> 00:09:45.360
Regimental Commander,
why don't we retreat for now ?

00:09:45.360 --> 00:09:46.950
And forsake the rewards ?

00:09:46.950 --> 00:09:47.610
But...

00:09:47.610 --> 00:09:48.520
Regimental Commander !

00:10:13.180 --> 00:10:18.630
Lt. Colonel Schenkopp, as I recall,
I left the base under your command.

00:10:20.360 --> 00:10:26.000
That's what I recall, too, but reality
sometimes supercedes memory.

00:10:27.100 --> 00:10:29.390
I came to help you
because you're incompetent.

00:10:30.660 --> 00:10:34.890
More importantly, Lt. Colonel, the
enemy seems to be closing in on us.

00:10:34.890 --> 00:10:35.900
How many ?

00:10:35.900 --> 00:10:41.660
I can't say for sure, but I'd say
more than 10 times our numbers.

00:10:41.660 --> 00:10:47.230
In my humble opinion, I think we should
withdraw before they surround us.

00:10:56.020 --> 00:11:01.050
He used to be well-regarded before
he became the regimental commander...

00:11:02.350 --> 00:11:04.450
...but as soon as
he became commander...

00:11:04.450 --> 00:11:09.450
...he became arrogant to his subordinates
and obsequious to his superiors.

00:11:10.800 --> 00:11:14.800
Well, I suppose he didn't
have the right mentality...

00:11:14.800 --> 00:11:17.890
...to make a successful adjustment
to his own advancement.

00:11:19.520 --> 00:11:21.690
We have no choice
but to withdraw.

00:11:21.690 --> 00:11:25.460
The soldiers from the disabled tank
should ride in the other vehicles.

00:11:25.850 --> 00:11:26.650
Hurry !

00:11:43.100 --> 00:11:44.060
What're you doing ?!

00:11:44.960 --> 00:11:48.350
Well, since it's too boring
to just self-destruct this vehicle...

00:11:48.350 --> 00:11:50.280
...I thought I'd
set up a booby trap.

00:11:51.040 --> 00:11:53.070
Of course, we can't expect
too great a result out of it.

00:12:18.580 --> 00:12:24.590
If the enemy truly is Luneberg, he'll just
ignore the trap and come right after us.

00:12:24.590 --> 00:12:28.000
In one-on-one combat, you'd
beat Luneberg, wouldn't you ?

00:12:29.600 --> 00:12:30.700
I don't know.

00:12:31.680 --> 00:12:36.310
Eight years ago, when I first
came into the Rosenritter...

00:12:36.310 --> 00:12:41.100
...I matched up with him in the semi-final
of an intra-squad close-combat tournament.

00:12:41.780 --> 00:12:43.150
Did you win ?

00:12:44.250 --> 00:12:46.660
If I had won, I wouldn't
have kept it in my memory.

00:12:46.660 --> 00:12:48.940
You lost...Lt. Colonel ?

00:12:49.700 --> 00:12:51.650
I was just a
2nd lieutenant back then.

00:12:51.650 --> 00:12:54.520
Luneberg was a captain.

00:12:56.970 --> 00:12:59.760
Eight years since then...

00:12:59.760 --> 00:13:02.930
I wonder how
strong he is now.

00:13:05.530 --> 00:13:08.150
Lt. Colonel, there's the
enemy, at 11 o'clock.

00:13:12.970 --> 00:13:14.300
We're surrounded.

00:13:14.300 --> 00:13:15.520
And being chased in.

00:13:16.880 --> 00:13:17.660
Damn.

00:13:17.660 --> 00:13:19.240
How nice.

00:13:20.320 --> 00:13:25.400
Stop your vehicles and surrender,
or else we'll open fire.

00:13:26.130 --> 00:13:28.700
That pisses me off.{It makes me mad.}
Why don't we talk back to them ?

00:13:28.700 --> 00:13:29.840
Incoming !

00:13:34.370 --> 00:13:35.960
Can't you at least
wait for our answer ?

00:14:49.440 --> 00:14:51.910
C...Colonel Luneberg...

00:14:56.780 --> 00:14:58.120
Lt. Colonel Schenkopp...

00:15:09.470 --> 00:15:10.900
Schenkopp.

00:15:14.200 --> 00:15:15.730
So you've become a Lt. Colonel.

00:15:16.540 --> 00:15:18.780
What a career you've had.

00:15:23.700 --> 00:15:26.560
And I heard you've gotten
the title of "Excellency" now.

00:15:26.560 --> 00:15:27.420
Good for you.

00:15:29.380 --> 00:15:32.870
The Empire doesn't have very many
talented commanders, that's why.

00:15:33.630 --> 00:15:37.790
You should wait till you become a
High Admiral to say stuff like that.

00:16:16.740 --> 00:16:21.350
I guess you've improved your close
combat skills a little bit, you little squirt.

00:16:21.350 --> 00:16:24.040
Yours have diminished
because your life of nobility.

00:17:42.750 --> 00:17:45.440
Blumhart, are you
trying to throw us off ?

00:17:45.440 --> 00:17:47.500
Do you actually have a
driver's license, Blumhart ?!

00:17:59.940 --> 00:18:04.810
Schenkopp, that fledgling,
he's gotten sharper.

00:18:04.810 --> 00:18:06.190
Your Excellency, should we pursue them ?

00:18:06.190 --> 00:18:07.800
That's unnecessary.

00:18:10.940 --> 00:18:14.570
It'll be troublesome if they
have substantial reinforcements.

00:18:14.570 --> 00:18:19.320
Besides, it's clear now that there's
an enemy base on this satellite.

00:18:19.320 --> 00:18:22.940
The present mission is to confirm
that fact, and we've done that.

00:18:22.940 --> 00:18:26.200
Plus, we've inflicted a severe injury
to the enemy's regimental commander...

00:18:26.200 --> 00:18:28.790
...and captured
four armored vehicles.

00:18:28.790 --> 00:18:31.150
That's more than
enough for results.

00:18:33.370 --> 00:18:38.340
Regardless, the combat style of the
Rosenritter has gotten so vulgar.

00:18:57.020 --> 00:18:59.000
Give him an antipyretic
and a pain killer.

00:19:00.200 --> 00:19:01.740
I don't want
a pain killer.

00:19:17.820 --> 00:19:21.310
The previous commander
beat the present commander.

00:19:23.530 --> 00:19:26.140
We should be ashamed.

00:19:39.060 --> 00:19:45.450
The Rosenritter's 12th regimental commander,
Colonel Otto Frank von Wahnschaffe...

00:19:45.450 --> 00:19:49.570
...was immediately sent to the military
hospital upon his arrival at the base...

00:19:49.570 --> 00:19:53.170
...but he did not have enough life
left to survive the operation...

00:19:53.170 --> 00:19:57.350
...and died at 6:40
on March 31st.

00:19:59.350 --> 00:20:02.810
He was the fourth casualty of the
Rosenritter regimental commanders.

00:20:08.550 --> 00:20:11.270
Are you saying that the Imperial
troops will attack our base ?

00:20:11.270 --> 00:20:14.700
Of course that's
what I'm saying.

00:20:16.740 --> 00:20:18.510
That's only logical, isn't it ?

00:20:19.350 --> 00:20:22.810
Unless Luneberg suddenly
develops a speech disorder...

00:20:22.810 --> 00:20:25.150
...he'll report our presence
to his superiors...

00:20:25.150 --> 00:20:28.780
...and their headquarters will give
orders to move their fleet in on us.

00:20:32.060 --> 00:20:36.980
Then why are you still standing
here and not preparing for battle ?

00:20:36.980 --> 00:20:40.450
I'm waiting for orders from you,
Your Excellency, Base Commander.

00:20:42.050 --> 00:20:47.210
Right now, I'm merely the
senior officer in the regiment.

00:20:47.210 --> 00:20:49.950
I need official authority.

00:20:51.700 --> 00:20:53.730
You want official rank,
at a time like this.

00:21:01.390 --> 00:21:03.800
I appoint Lt. Colonel
Walter von Schenkopp...

00:21:03.800 --> 00:21:07.420
...as interim commander of
the Rosenritter Regiment.

00:21:09.570 --> 00:21:13.910
I don't care for the rank, but I need
the authority to give out orders.

00:21:22.540 --> 00:21:28.360
Oh, yes, I think you should request
reinforcements from our fleet.

00:21:29.360 --> 00:21:33.130
Of course, you probably
already know that, I trust.

00:21:39.320 --> 00:21:43.700
I don't particularly think of it as payback
for the death of Colonel Wahnschaffe...

00:21:43.700 --> 00:21:46.450
...but I should settle matters
with Luneberg, regardless.

00:21:47.280 --> 00:21:49.660
But I suppose the
opportunity will soon arrive.

00:21:56.900 --> 00:22:00.750
But this is such
a useless army.

00:22:00.750 --> 00:22:06.660
Will I ever meet a competent
commander before I retire or die ?

00:22:22.940 --> 00:22:26.730
The communication shuttle that went to
the 5th Fleet hasn't returned yet, has it ?

00:22:26.730 --> 00:22:29.310
What's happening ?

00:22:44.770 --> 00:22:49.080
Admiral, it's an emergency communication
from our rear-line base on Van-Fleet 4-2.

00:22:51.500 --> 00:22:53.420
How did it get to us ?

00:22:53.420 --> 00:22:59.130
We happened to pass near Van-Fleet 4
when the transmission was made.

00:23:02.600 --> 00:23:06.400
A fleet from the Imperial naval
forces is at Van-Fleet 4-2 ?

00:23:07.340 --> 00:23:09.040
They're asking for help.

00:23:10.810 --> 00:23:12.700
What should we do ?

00:23:12.700 --> 00:23:15.190
But why a rear-line base ?

00:23:15.190 --> 00:23:18.150
And they're sending
an entire fleet.

00:23:18.150 --> 00:23:19.570
I don't understand
their intentions.

00:23:19.570 --> 00:23:21.610
It could be a trap.

00:23:21.610 --> 00:23:23.250
One fleet as a decoy ?

00:23:23.250 --> 00:23:26.800
If the Empire has someone who has a
knack for enormous strategic conception...

00:23:26.800 --> 00:23:29.930
...they might prepare
such a trap.

00:23:29.930 --> 00:23:33.660
Then should we ignore it and continue
on with our present strategy ?

00:23:36.270 --> 00:23:40.860
Though Bucock is gifted with
a flexible and open mind...

00:23:40.860 --> 00:23:44.640
...he was essentially a tactician
and not a strategist.

00:23:44.640 --> 00:23:46.750
In accordance with that
personality, he made a decision.

00:23:47.610 --> 00:23:51.030
All ships, we'll head at full
speed for Van-Fleet 4-2.

00:23:51.030 --> 00:23:51.650
Yes, sir.

00:23:52.450 --> 00:23:53.860
Change of course.

00:23:53.860 --> 00:23:57.780
The destination,
Van-Fleet 4, 2nd satellite.

00:23:57.780 --> 00:24:00.090
All ships, advance at full speed.

00:24:00.530 --> 00:24:04.040
Rear Admiral, this may
start out as just a skirmish...

00:24:04.040 --> 00:24:07.190
...but it could turn out to
be the beginning of a storm...

00:24:07.190 --> 00:24:14.480
...like the center of a low
atmospheric pressure system.

00:24:14.950 --> 00:24:19.540
I'd like to be alive to
see what comes out of it.

00:24:24.240 --> 00:24:31.750
How Bucock's decision would influence the
outcome of the battle on Van-Fleet 4-2...

00:24:31.750 --> 00:24:34.590
...no one could
predict at this stage.

00:24:37.940 --> 00:24:46.150
Defectors

